    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## **Complete the Action Filter**\r\n\r\nWhen the user clicks **Action**, only movies with the genre **Action** should appear.\r\n\r\n#### **Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Use AI to help you complete the `filterActionMovies` function.\r\n\r\n2. In the function, use `.map()` to go through each movie in `movies`.\r\n\r\n3. Inside the `.map()`, use an `if` statement to check whether the movie’s genre is `\"Action\"`.\r\n\r\n4. If the movie’s genre is `\"Action\"`, use `.push()` to add that movie to `displayMovies`.\r\n\r\n5. Call `renderMovies()` as the last line of the `filterActionMovies` function.\r\n\r\n6. Use your function as the event handler for the **Action** button.",
